"""Build a static report from retrieved metadata; no image processing."""
import html, json
from pathlib import Path
root=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[3]
run=root/"runs/hemp-residual-segmentation-v1"
r=json.loads((run/"results/report.json").read_text())
rows=[]
for x in r["arms"]:
 m=x["metrics"]
 rows.append(f"<tr><td>{html.escape(x['arm'])}</td><td>{x['inference_calls']}</td><td>{m['final_foreground_coverage']:.1%}</td><td>{m['residual_foreground_coverage']:.1%}</td><td>{m['new_definite_background_pixels']}</td><td>{m['background_fraction_of_final_prediction']:.2%}</td><td>{x['accepted_proposals']}</td><td>{x['edge_accepted_proposals']}</td><td>{x['cross_crop_duplicate_pairs_iou_ge_0_5']}</td></tr>")
cards=''.join(f"<figure><img src='results/{x['arm']}/overlay.png'><figcaption>{html.escape(x['arm'])}: blue initial acceptance; green new proxy coverage; red still uncovered; amber leakage.</figcaption></figure>" for x in r['arms'])
closeups=''.join(f"<figure><img src='results/closeups/{region}--{arm}-instances.png'><figcaption>{region}: {arm} individual second-pass proposals</figcaption></figure>" for region in ['upper-left-fan','central-overlap','lower-right-drooping-fan'] for arm in ['black-fill','original-context-residual'])
doc=f"""<!doctype html><meta charset=utf-8><title>Residual SAM3 A/B</title><style>body{{font:16px system-ui;max-width:1100px;margin:2rem auto;background:#10151b;color:#e8edf2}}a{{color:#72b7ff}}table{{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}}td,th{{padding:.55rem;border:1px solid #52606d}}.cards{{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:1rem}}img{{width:100%;image-rendering:auto}}small{{color:#b8c2cc}}</style><h1>Residual SAM3 matched-budget comparison</h1><p><b>Foreground-proxy result:</b> original-context crops improve final coverage from 30.47% to 31.94% (+1.47 percentage points); black-fill reaches 30.77% (+0.30 points). This modest gain comes with more duplicate and crop-edge proposals.</p><p><b>Source limitation:</b> {html.escape(r['input_label'])}. Detached-shoot images were rejected. Initial masks are provisionally frozen automated score≥0.5 proposals, not human-accepted labels. All figures use a foreground color proxy and are not ground-truth accuracy or leaf counts. The newly found living/potted source was reviewed separately and was not tested here.</p><table><tr><th>Arm</th><th>Calls</th><th>Final proxy coverage</th><th>New residual coverage</th><th>Addition-only bg px</th><th>Final bg fraction</th><th>Accepted proposals</th><th>Edge-truncated</th><th>Duplicate pairs</th></tr>{''.join(rows)}</table><div class=cards>{cards}</div><h2>Boundary review</h2><p>The individual-proposal views show partial blades and crop-edge fragments. Black-fill produced almost no accepted additions at 0.5 and did not restore the missed upper-left fan. The static residual-mass scheduler heavily repeats dense regions; this tests that selector, not all context-preserving strategies. These are fixed calibration ROIs, not held-out ground truth.</p><div class=cards>{closeups}</div><h2>Bounded alternatives</h2><p><a href='results/alternatives/visual-exemplar/result.json'>Visual-region box prompting</a> uses the same checkpoint with three broad calibration rectangles. The corrected <a href='results/alternatives/point-refinement/result.json'>six-prompt point-refinement test</a> isolated small local blade regions for the highest predicted-IoU candidates. It is oracle-assisted interactive review, not autonomous discovery. Earlier failed attempts are retained as implementation errors.</p><small>Threshold 0.5, prompt “leaf”, crop 48×56, 87 calls per arm. Equal call count does not assert equal compute. Proxy metrics are descriptive only.</small>"""
(run/"index.html").write_text(doc)
